{"title":"1998 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded7c7889e0b07d887213007e12361710d64a300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(-3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb916b0a81a1744de94ec93f890857f701d22a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(5, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f606276339118d44b2d35b2b4a4d95bab37e2399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(8, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The base of the triangle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c53db830ee6704b5c415f12c89a2b04690aa19f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - (-3) = 5 + 3 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" /> and the height would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee068e9ec1a1408fec805621db65ada911fda40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4ae681c4cf5ec73b7d8dc2a5fa638e9da45ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{1}{2}bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the base of the triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the height of the triangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the area of the triangle. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b6983ec1375fc0dcb56f660b8ed96a0abb33669b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times 6 = 4 \\times 6 = \\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"234\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017191502\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 51/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2017/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.529      1 1998_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    7.529      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36599:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017191502 and revision id 282433. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}